{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["Now he said <b>at the end of the days.</b> These are the days of the Messiah, which are the end of the days of the world. <b>And it shall be, etc.</b> Now there were no days after Isaiah in which there were no wars, and this is written in the book of Ben Gurion and in the books of Persia and Media <small>(variant: and Rome)</small>, for war did not cease in the Second Temple, and furthermore Scripture testified: 'and they shall no longer learn [war].'" "<b>[established, etc.].</b> We know that the Temple Mount will not literally be <b>raised up</b>; rather its meaning: the Temple Mount will be established, so that they will run to it from the four directions as though it were higher than all the hills." "<b>And they shall stream.</b> From the root נהר [river], on account of its flowing."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Resolved ונהרו in comment 0 as the concluding phrase; the citation 'ולא ילמדו עוד' appears truncated without its continuation 'מלחמה' (Isaiah 2:4)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:34.432905137Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}